<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX DE L'ARC DE TRIOMPHE RECORDS/STATISTICS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX DE L'ARC DE TRIOMPHE RECORDS/STATISTICS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Records and statistics associated</p>
<p>with Sunday's Prix de l'Arc de Triomphe horse race:</p>
<p>Dual winners: - Ksar (1921-22), Motrico (1930, 1932),</p>
<p>Corrida (1936-37), Tantieme  (1950-51), Ribot (1955-56), Alleged</p>
<p>(1977-78)</p>
<p>Greatest winning margin: Six lengths, by Ribot (1956) and</p>
<p>Sea Bird (1965)</p>
<p>Female winners (15): Pearl Cap (1931), Samos (1935), Corrida</p>
<p>(1936-37), Nikellora (1945), Coronation (1949), La Sorellina</p>
<p>(1953), San San (1972), Allez France (1974), Ivanjica (1976),</p>
<p>Three Troikas (1979), Detroit (1980), Gold River (1981), Akiyda</p>
<p>(1982), All Along (1983), Urban Sea (1993)</p>
<p>Grey winners: Biribi (1926) and Migoli (1948)</p>
<p>Longest priced winner: 119-1 Star Appeal (1979)</p>
<p>Shortest priced winners: 3-10 Ksar (1922), Caracalla (1946)</p>
<p>Oldest winner: Motrico (seven) in 1932.</p>
<p>Three winners have been awarded the race in the stewards'</p>
<p>room:  Cadum (1925), Saint Crespin (1959) (dead-heated with</p>
<p>Midnight Sun but the latter was demoted to second for</p>
<p>hampering), Rainbow Quest (1985)</p>
<p>British-trained winners (9). Comrade (1920), Parth (1923),</p>
<p>Migoli (1948), Mill Reef (1971), Rheingold (1973), Rainbow Quest</p>
<p>(1985), Dancing Brave (1986), Carroll House (1989) and Lammtarra</p>
<p>(1995)</p>
<p>Irish-trained winners: Ballymoss (1958), Levmoss (1969) and</p>
<p>Alleged (1977-78)</p>
<p>Italian-trained winners: Ortello (1929), Crapom (1933),</p>
<p>Ribot (1955-56), Molvedo (1961) and Tony Bin (1988).</p>
<p>German-trained winner: Star Appeal (1975)</p>
<p>Fastest Arc: Trempolino (1987) 2 minutes 26.3 seconds.</p>
<p>Largest field: 30 (1967)</p>
<p>Smallest field: 7 (1941)</p>
<p>Most successful trainers (4 wins each): Charles Semblat,</p>
<p>Alec Head and Francois Mathet.</p>
<p>Most successful jockeys (4 wins each): Jacko Doyasbere,</p>
<p>Freddie Head, Yves Saint-Martin and Pat Eddery.</p>
